WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.064
In the late Southern Song, Xiangyang and Fancheng were the Song's important defense against the great Mongol army, their walls tall and strong.

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:16.406
The two cities faced each other across the Han River, guarding this defense line together.

00:00:16.756 --> 00:00:22.972
The Mongol army surrounded Xiangyang completely, and the siege lasted for years.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:31.506
The Mongols brought new weapons; tall trebuchets kept hurling huge stones at the walls.

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:37.112
The Song soldiers inside fought desperately, but the relief army they hoped for never came.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:43.030
They gazed into the distance, still holding on to a last thread of hope.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.844
In the year 1273, Xiangyang finally fell.

00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:55.754
After Xiangyang fell, the Southern Song's Yangtze defense collapsed, hastening the dynasty's fall.

00:00:56.104 --> 00:01:00.664
This long war changed the fate of many people.

